      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْرَجُ</span></b> , in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْرَجُ الثَّنَايَا</span>, <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْلَجُ</span> [q. v.].
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And A man <i>whose buttocks do not meet,</i> (S,
O, K,) or <i>scarcely meet,</i> (TA,) <i>by reason of their
bigness:</i> (S, O, K:) fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرْجَآءُ</span>: it is mostly the
case among the Abyssinians. (S, O.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرِجٌ</span>.

